    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0826" n="1660" xml:id="pg1660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/475</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-28T14:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 28, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 29, 6.15
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1025. Department’s 848, January 26, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d702-f1"/>
                    Belmont replies as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In very general way tonnage question has been discussed here and should
                            be taken up later by competent representatives [familiar with?]
                            practices now in force in the United States. Certain facilities apart
                            from agreement now under consideration are likely to be secured at a
                            northern port, but in meantime whatever use you have made of bunker
                            licenses to influence routing and obtaining tonnage should be used
                            discreetly as suggested in Embassy’s 1007, January 20, 6 p.m. [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">21, 10 a.m.</hi>]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d702-f2"
                            /> Had no intention of conveying advice to make sweeping use of bunker
                            coaling as pressure. This would irritate and embarrass situation.
                            Advantageous moment in view of sinkings of Spanish ships to get into
                            closer relations. Belmont.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
